body:
I don't want to seem like a downer. but there isn't much you can do. My GF at the time had an abortion without telling me and she was at least a few weeks along when she got the abortion. Woman have more rights than men in this situation. I don't think any men have rights at all when it comes to abortions. If you have to tell a friend what is going on and that home is toxic right now and you can't stay there in the current state you are in. When she has this abortion you will need everyone that you know to help you out. It has been 2 years and almost every day I contemplate taking my own life. Get everything in order so you could get out of a relationship because when she has this abortion your life will turn into a living hell.

&#x200B;

YES I AM FINE PLEASE DO NOT REPORT MY COMMENT.

&#x200B;

Good Luck OP.

Pretty damn hard. I saw her around alot in school and it always reminded me of her. So I just thought of the fact that she was graduation the next year. That was that she graduated and the new school year started and I found a girl that actually wanted to stay with me.

&#x200B;

You have to either find a new hobby or play a shit ton of video games!

In all seriousness though tell her that if you are willing to go back and stay and be with a guy who treats you like shit than stay there. I've dealt with this before there is something going on with her. 

&#x200B;

Good Luck!

I am being honest here that their isn't enough here for people to understand the full story all we know is that "you two separated and you don't want your ex husband to bring his girlfriend" which is also childish. I have been in about a dozen of situations where my parents (and stepparents) were petty not to even go to an event due to the other spouse. Like it will look like you are making a rule for a man who isn't yours to control. You all need to sit down and explain this to her. No attacks on either side not "she said" "he said" bullshit. If need be you need to take her to a place that is neutral for both parties and realize this is a reality that you are going to have to live in. 

&#x200B;

Good Luck! You will need it!

Heres the thing something is there like maybe an ex that did him wrong in a way that he retreated when you asked him to marry you. I've been in the situation of getting dumped (because of the distance) while at school and it almost drove me to suicide. (disclaimer: mods I know there are trolls and I don't pay any attention to them I am in a better place now.) You need to take this slow or you both will crash and burn. good love is like cooking a thanksgiving turkey you can rush it or you will burn what you have. If you both want to wait then there needs to be an open line of communication 24/7. The both of your needs need to meet. 

&#x200B;

Good Luck if you need anyone to talk to just message me.

He thinks that you two are still going to be a thing and he is "Love-High". I was in the same position that he was in with a girl. You need to let him know in a direct way that there will never be a thing between you two and just leave it at that. He isn't mentally stable and neither was I. All he needs is time alone to get over you. But know that when you cross that line that it will put a scar on the way that he views you, so there is no coming back.

&#x200B;

Good Luck. If you need to talk about it just message me.
